# Adding a new class group — repeatable checklist

Use this every time you onboard a new class. No need to ask for a rebuild —
just follow these steps with the three template files.

Pick your two values first, e.g.:
  __CLASS_NAME__   ->  QE2501A
  __BUCKET_NAME__  ->  students-photo-qe2501a   (lowercase, matches your convention)

---

## 1. Create the storage bucket
Supabase Dashboard -> Storage -> New bucket
  Name: __BUCKET_NAME__   (exact spelling matters — case-sensitive)
  Public bucket: OFF

## 2. Run the storage policy SQL
Open `new_class_storage_policy.sql`, find-and-replace:
  __CLASS_NAME__  -> your class name
  __BUCKET_NAME__ -> your bucket name
Paste the result into Supabase SQL Editor and run it.

(No table changes needed — `students` and `archive_attendance` already
have a shared `class` column and RLS policies from the multi-class setup.)

## 3. Migrate the roster
- Open the Google Sheet for this class (must have Name / Photo_URL columns
  in a tab, default name "Attendance").
- Extensions -> Apps Script.
- Paste in `migrate_template.gs`, find-and-replace __CLASS_NAME__ and
  __BUCKET_NAME__ throughout.
- Fill in SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY (same values you already
  use for every other class — one Supabase project for everyone).
- Adjust SHEET_NAME if this sheet's tab isn't literally named "Attendance".
- Run migrateAllStudents. If you see "TIME BUDGET REACHED — RUN AGAIN TO
  CONTINUE", just click Run again — it resumes automatically, skipping
  anyone already migrated. Repeat until you see "MIGRATION COMPLETE".
- If you hit an OAuth authorization prompt the first time, click through
  it (Review permissions -> Advanced -> Go to [project] (unsafe) -> Allow)
  — normal for a script that's never run in this Google account before.

## 4. Deploy the camera page
- Open `camera_template.html`, find-and-replace __CLASS_NAME__ and
  __BUCKET_NAME__ throughout.
- Fill in SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_ANON_KEY (same anon key used
  everywhere else — safe to reuse, RLS is what actually restricts access).
- Save it as `camera-<classname-lowercase>.html`, e.g. camera-qe2501a.html
- Upload to your GitHub Pages repo, same folder as the others.

## 5. Add it to the launcher
Open `index.html`, duplicate one of the existing lines in the `.links` div:
  <a class="launch primary" href="camera-qe2501a.html">▶️ Take Attendance — QE2501A</a>
Commit.

## 6. (Already works — no action needed)
`archive.html`'s Class dropdown pulls from a hardcoded option list. If you
want the new class selectable there too, open archive.html and add one
line inside the <select id="filterClass"> block:
  <option value="__CLASS_NAME__">__CLASS_NAME__</option>

---

## Sanity check before calling it done
- [ ] Bucket exists and photos are visible in Supabase Storage
- [ ] Table Editor -> students shows the new class's rows with the
      correct `class` value and non-empty `photo_path`
- [ ] camera-<classname>.html loads, Load Students detects faces
      (check browser console for any "No face detected in: X" —
      those specific students' source photos may need retaking)
- [ ] Marking someone present updates the absentee list AND shows up
      in archive.html filtered to that class
- [ ] The old classes' camera pages still only show their own students
      (each camera page's CLASS_NAME must be genuinely unique per class,
      matching what you used in step 3/4 exactly — a typo here is the
      most common cause of classes bleeding into each other)
